WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:09.465
Catering trays, cake orders, coffee for the office: Order Tracking follows every customer order, so nobody has to ask what’s due, or who’s on it.

2
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:17.445
Open Order Tracking. The board has a column for each stage: new, confirmed, in progress, ready, and on the way.

3
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:24.449
Each card shows the customer, what they ordered, when it’s due, and who’s on it. Late orders are outlined in red.

4
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.828
The muffins are ready. Click Move to Ready on the card, or drag it to the next column.

5
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:39.419
Pick a store at the top to see just its board, and who’s on duty there. If you use Square, that store’s Square orders show alongside yours, with a Square tag.

6
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:46.501
To add an order, click New order. For a quick one at the counter, choose Walk-in, so there’s no customer to look up.

7
00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:54.561
Add the items, and Worklynq works out the total. Choose pickup or delivery, when it’s due, and who’s on it. Then create the order.

8
00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:03.311
Click any order to open it. The stage bar moves it along, and the history shows every change, who made it, and any notes.

9
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:14.020
Completed shows how the day or week went: orders, revenue, what sold best, and who did the work. You can export it, or ask Assist, like which days were busiest.

10
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:22.995
That’s Order Tracking. Next in the Features series: inventory. You’ll find every guide at worklynq.com/docs.

